# Graduate Master's Chemical Engineering Curricular Architecture
#
# Master of Science (M.S.) & Master of Engineering (M.Eng.) in Chemical Engineering: advanced transport, molecular thermodynamics, and process systems.

#>spw_cache_univ_masters_cheme
#:cache #!chemical_engineering
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Model the graduate Master of Science (M.S.) and Master of Engineering (M.Eng.) curricula in Chemical Engineering, articulating advanced continuum transport, molecular thermodynamics, catalytic microkinetics, and dynamic process optimization."
  ~#degree_tracks: "Thesis Track (M.S. in Chemical Engineering) and Professional Practicum Track (M.Eng. in Chemical Engineering)"
}

^["advanced_continuum_transport_phenomena"]{
  graduate_depth: "Rigorous vector-tensor analysis of momentum, energy, and multicomponent mass transport (Bird-Stewart-Lightfoot formalism)."
  transport_pillars: #[
    "Stress Tensors & Invariant Formulations: Cauchy stress tensor, constitutive equations for Newtonian and non-Newtonian fluids (Bingham plastics, power-law, viscoelastic Maxwell models)",
    "Exact Solutions & Asymptotic Scaling: Creeping flow (Stokes flow past a sphere), lubrication approximation in thin films, and boundary layer similarity solutions (Blasius flow)",
    "Turbulent Transport Physics: Reynolds decomposition, turbulent Reynolds stresses, eddy viscosity models, k-epsilon closures, and mixing-length hypotheses",
    "Multicomponent Diffusion Dynamics: Maxwell-Stefan equations for non-dilute multicomponent mixtures, generalized Fick's law, and thermo-diffusion (Soret effect)"
  ]
}

^["molecular_thermodynamics_and_phase_equilibria"]{
  graduate_thermo: "Statistical mechanical foundations and advanced equations of state for non-ideal industrial mixtures."
  thermodynamic_frameworks: .{
    molecular_eos: #[
      "Cubic Equations of State: Advanced mixing rules for Peng-Robinson (PR) and Soave-Redlich-Kwong (SRK) with Huron-Vidal mixing rules",
      "Statistical Associating Fluid Theory (SAFT): Modeling chain formation, association hydrogen-bonding sites, and polar interactions",
      "Activity Coefficient Models: Local composition models (NRTL, UNIQUAC) and predictive UNIFAC group contribution methods"
    ]
    multiphase_equilibria: "Rigorous algorithms for Vapor-Liquid-Liquid Equilibria (VLLE), azeotropic phase behavior, retrograde condensation, and polymer-solvent phase separation"
    interfacial_thermodynamics: "Surface tension, Gibbs adsorption isotherm, contact angle hysteresis, and Marangoni interfacial flow phenomena"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["heterogeneous_catalysis_and_microkinetics"]{
  reaction_frontiers: "Rational catalyst design and multi-scale kinetic modeling."
  catalytic_principles: #[
    "Surface Reaction Mechanisms: Langmuir-Hinshelwood, Eley-Rideal, and Mars-van Krevelen redox mechanisms on solid metal/metal-oxide surfaces",
    "Microkinetic Analysis: Elementary surface reaction steps without rate-determining step assumptions, utilizing transition-state scaling relations (Brønsted-Evans-Polanyi)",
    "Transport-Reaction Coupling: Internal pore diffusion limitations, generalized Thiele modulus for arbitrary kinetics, Weisz-Prater criterion, and effectiveness factors",
    "Catalyst Deactivation & Regeneration: Modeling coking, sulfur poisoning, hydrothermal sintering, and continuous moving-bed regeneration"
  ]
}

^["process_systems_engineering_and_optimization"]{
  computational_engineering: "Dynamic optimization, model predictive control, and plant-wide synthesis."
  optimization_methods: .{
    dynamic_control: "Nonlinear Model Predictive Control (NMPC), state estimation via Extended Kalman Filters (EKF), and moving horizon estimation (MHE)"
    mathematical_programming: "Formulation of Mixed-Integer Linear Programming (MILP) and Mixed-Integer Nonlinear Programming (MINLP) for flowsheet synthesis"
    energy_integration: "Pinch Analysis for heat exchanger networks (HEN), grand composite curves, and minimum utility requirement targets"
    uncertainty_quantification: "Robust optimization accounting for feedstock composition variability and fluctuating electricity pricing"
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["sustainable_energy_and_electrochemical_engineering"]{
  modern_specializations: #[
    "Electrochemical Systems: Butler-Volmer kinetics, Nernst-Planck ion transport, PEM water electrolysis, and lithium-ion battery degradation modeling",
    "Carbon Management Technologies: Direct air capture (DAC), post-combustion amine scrubbing, and industrial CO2 electrochemical reduction",
    "Bioprocess Engineering: Microbial growth kinetics (Monod model), gas-liquid mass transfer (kLa) in industrial stirred fermenters, and downstream chromatography scaling"
  ]
}

^["taste"]{
  ~#taste: "Master's-level chemical engineering is the supreme art of scaling: mastering the invisible nano-scale dance of surface molecules to dictate the behavior of megawatt-scale industrial infrastructure."
  ~#wonder: "Why does the Maxwell-Stefan formulation succeed in predicting multicomponent diffusion barriers where classical Fickian intuition fails entirely?"

  principles: #[
    "Transport is unified: Momentum, heat, and mass share the same differential DNA; master the flux equation and you master them all.",
    "Optimization requires humility: An optimal flowsheet on paper will fail in practice if it cannot dynamically reject unmeasured disturbances.",
    "The green transition demands mass-balance rigor: There are no energetic free lunches; every decarbonization technology must account for full lifecycle mass and energy."
  ]
}

^"invariants"{
  "Graduate theses in chemical engineering must demonstrate quantitative validation against either experimental data or verified asymptotic analytical solutions.",
  "Process optimization models must satisfy Second-Law thermodynamic constraints (positive entropy generation across all boundary envelopes).",
  "Design of electrochemical or reactive systems must explicitly account for coupled mass transport limitations alongside intrinsic surface kinetics.",
}

#>wonder_masters_cheme_1
?["How does the integration of neural ordinary differential equations (Neural-ODEs) into NMPC controllers improve chemical reactor yield under stochastic feedstock variations?"]{
  #:depth #!engineering ~#lens(data_driven_control)
  ~#hypothesis: "Neural-ODE augmented model predictive controllers achieve 18% higher product selectivity in highly exothermic polymerizations compared to standard linearized state-space controllers by accurately capturing fast unmodeled thermal transients."
  !probe{ "Conduct hardware-in-the-loop pilot plant testing comparing Neural-ODE control against standard industrial PID and linear MPC across 50 feedstock disturbance cycles." }
  $%[control.reactor_selectivity_percent, safety.peak_temperature_overshoot_kelvin]
}
